  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The incorrect statement from the following for borazine is:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "It contains banana bonds",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<p>It can react with water</p>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p>It is a cyclic compound</p>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p>It has electronic delocalization</p>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The statement &quot;It contains a banana bond&quot; is incorrect about Borazine.</p><p>Borazine, also known as inorganic benzene or borazole, is a chemical compound with the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>. Borazine is a hexagonal planar molecule with alternating boron and nitrogen atoms, and it exhibits some structural and chemical similarities to benzene.&nbsp;Borazine is an aromatic compound with electron&nbsp;delocalization. It does not contain banana bond.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0027_99637a93e623.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 335px;\" /></p><p>On heating, borazine hydrolyses slowly.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>"
  }
